his city was visited by Arjuna in search of the dead child of a द्वारका Bra1hman2a;
5: Ib. X. ८९. ४४; Br. IV. ३३. ६७.
Born of आकाश: the wind-god loved अञ्जना and gave birth to हनुमान्: overlord of the winds, formless creatures and of time. Presiding deity of Bhuvarloka and hence Bhuvas- pati (also मातरिश्व). Addressed by the sages engaged in sacrifice to speak on लोकालोक;
6: Ib. II. २०. 1 and 7; २५. 5-१४;

